Case Study 42: Student Marks Matrix Analysis
1. Problem Statement
Analyse student marks stored in a nested list and calculate each student's total and average.
2. Objectives
•	Represent marks using nested lists.
•	Calculate row-wise totals and averages.
•	Find the highest total.
3. Algorithm
37.	Store student names and marks in lists.
38.	For each student, calculate total and average.
39.	Compare totals to find the highest scorer.
40.	Display the results.
4. Python Source Code
names = ["Anu", "Ravi", "Sita"]
marks = [[80, 70, 90], [60, 75, 65], [90, 85, 95]]
highest = 0
top_student = ""

for i in range(len(names)):
    total = sum(marks[i])
    average = total / len(marks[i])
    print(names[i], "total:", total, "average:", average)

    if total > highest:
        highest = total
        top_student = names[i]

print("Top student:", top_student)
print("Highest total:", highest)
5. Sample Output
Anu total: 240 average: 80.0
Ravi total: 200 average: 66.66666666666667
Sita total: 270 average: 90.0
Top student: Sita
Highest total: 270
6. Test Cases
